Hi @vvenkataramani @mjain,

The DAS specification v2.2 (header "E" file + employee "S" file, per the CNAS télédéclaration guide) is ready: [link]. It covers:
- one E/S file pair per CNAS employer number (one per location);
- file names D + YY + E/S + 10-digit CNAS employer number + .TXT;
- Employer No. on every record;
- Observation left blank;
- quarterly duration in days (0–92). The layout has no separators, so the date of birth is always followed directly by the Q1 duration; the "143J" value is the error, not the position.

To complete the Henkel set-up, please confirm for Reghaia and Chelghoum Laid (and confirm the values we took from the 2024 file for Dely Ibrahim): CNAS employer number, paying centre (centre payeur), denomination and address as registered with CNAS, and which employees belong to each location. Please also confirm the duration unit: "J" (days), as in the 2024 file, or "M" (months), as the CNAS guide indicates for monthly-paid staff.

@mjain please confirm the pay elements for the quarterly CNAS base (64551) and for unpaid absences (63121, 63122, 63129, 63801).

Regards,
